'''Angelic Sleipnir''' (天使スレイプニール, ''Tenshi Sureipunīru'', '''Angelic Sleipnir''') is an [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] enemy that appears in [[Legend Stages]]. He was added in [[Version 3.2 Update|Version 3.2]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Angelic Sleipnir
|image = E 125.png
|first appearance = '''SoL''': [[Subtle Curfew|Sub-chapter 21 - Subtle Curfew]]
|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[Weedy Garden|Sub-chapter 14 - Weedy Garden]]
|money drop = 905¢ - 3,575¢
}}

==Enemy==
Angelic Sleipnir has a very fast and fairly powerful attack along with high health and range, but moves slowly. He has a small chance to [[Knockback|knockback]] your cats, making him very deadly against poorly-prepared setups, and doubly so in stages where he acts as support, such as [[No Plan A (Deadly)|No Plan A]] and [[New Testament (Deadly)|New Testament]].

==Strategy==
The best way to deal with this enemy is to tank his attacks with [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]] combined with cats that outrange Sleipnir, such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]], [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], his [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed]] counterpart or [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance Cats]]. Rushers like Awakened Bahamut Cat can also work well, but they are not reliable as they typically have less range than Sleipnir, whose damage or knockback may simply stunlock them. Do not rely on [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], as she can't hit even once due to her inferior range and low health. Later on this enemy is used more often as backline support, meaning that it would be more practical to use the aforementioned Cats with Long Distance and other snipers to reach the backline.

